    "['isis enable [parameter1]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set protocols isis interface <interface-name>', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the Juniper equivalent of the HUAWEI command `isis enable 1` for interface configuration:\\n\\n##\\nset protocols isis interface <interface-name>\\n##\\n\\nNotes:\\n1. In Juniper, you would replace `<interface-name>` with the actual interface name (e.g., `ge-1/0/0.0` for GigabitEthernet1/0/0)\\n2. Unlike Huawei where you specify the IS-IS instance (1), Juniper typically doesn't require instance specification for basic IS-IS configurations\\n3. The Juniper command enables IS-IS on the interface but doesn't explicitly show the process ID like Huawei does\", 'trans_template': 'set protocols isis interface <interface-name>'}]]": 1,
    "['isis enable [parameter1]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set protocols isis interface ge-1/0/0.0', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': '##\\nset protocols isis interface ge-1/0/0.0\\nset protocols isis interface ge-2/0/0.0\\nset protocols isis interface lo0.1\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n1. In Juniper, enabling IS-IS on an interface is done by adding the interface under the IS-IS protocol configuration. \\n2. The \".0\" suffix is added for physical interfaces (ge-1/0/0.0) and \".1\" for loopback (lo0.1) as this is Juniper\\'s standard naming convention.\\n3. Unlike Huawei where you enable IS-IS with a process number (1), Juniper doesn\\'t require specifying the process number in the basic interface assignment.\\n\\nNote: The Juniper configuration assumes IS-IS is already globally enabled (equivalent to Huawei\\'s `isis 1` at the global level). If you need the full equivalent configuration including the IS-IS process setup, please let me know.', 'trans_template': 'set protocols isis interface ge-1/0/0.0'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set protocols isis interface ge-2/0/0.0', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': '##\\nset protocols isis interface ge-1/0/0.0\\nset protocols isis interface ge-2/0/0.0\\nset protocols isis interface lo0.1\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n1. In Juniper, enabling IS-IS on an interface is done by adding the interface under the IS-IS protocol configuration. \\n2. The \".0\" suffix is added for physical interfaces (ge-1/0/0.0) and \".1\" for loopback (lo0.1) as this is Juniper\\'s standard naming convention.\\n3. Unlike Huawei where you enable IS-IS with a process number (1), Juniper doesn\\'t require specifying the process number in the basic interface assignment.\\n\\nNote: The Juniper configuration assumes IS-IS is already globally enabled (equivalent to Huawei\\'s `isis 1` at the global level). If you need the full equivalent configuration including the IS-IS process setup, please let me know.', 'trans_template': 'set protocols isis interface ge-2/0/0.0'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set protocols isis interface lo0.1', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': '##\\nset protocols isis interface ge-1/0/0.0\\nset protocols isis interface ge-2/0/0.0\\nset protocols isis interface lo0.1\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n1. In Juniper, enabling IS-IS on an interface is done by adding the interface under the IS-IS protocol configuration. \\n2. The \".0\" suffix is added for physical interfaces (ge-1/0/0.0) and \".1\" for loopback (lo0.1) as this is Juniper\\'s standard naming convention.\\n3. Unlike Huawei where you enable IS-IS with a process number (1), Juniper doesn\\'t require specifying the process number in the basic interface assignment.\\n\\nNote: The Juniper configuration assumes IS-IS is already globally enabled (equivalent to Huawei\\'s `isis 1` at the global level). If you need the full equivalent configuration including the IS-IS process setup, please let me know.', 'trans_template': 'set protocols isis interface lo0.1'}]]": 1,
